  "note": "Two-column body page, 1750x2180 (ratio 0.803), not A4. No chapter banner, no page_header_band and no footer_rule. Strongly asymmetric: the ENTIRE left column is one tall pink worked-problems panel running y 0.119-0.928 and holding Problems 2.10 and 2.11 (blocks 1-15), while the right column carries the running body text (blocks 16-25). The panel is reported as its own box element with n:null; its fifteen interior blocks each carry the pink fill #f9c2d3 they sit on, sampled from the flat panel interior away from glyphs and edges - the same pink as p015's problem panels. The panel is closed top and bottom by a plain grey rule (approx #808080) that is part of the box's own border, NOT a footer_rule, so it is not given its own element. Each displayed expression inside the panel gets its own equation region as instructed (blocks 3, 6, 9, 11, 13, 15); block 6 is a four-line chain for nu and lambda and block 3 a two-line chain, each kept as one region because the input models each as one block. Block 8 is the bare bold word 'Solution' and is recorded as a paragraph at body size in serif-bold, the only element on the page where the bold label is a block of its own. Chapter-wide heading convention used across this batch, stated because the allowed list has only two heading roles for three printed levels: numbered headings are major_heading (here 2.4.2 and 2.5.1 at size_rel 1.15 and the top-level all-caps 2.5 at 1.2), unnumbered italic blue headings are section_heading (none on this page). Elements are listed with the left panel first, matching the input's block order, although the right column is in fact the continuation of the body prose from p020 and the panel is an aside. The last element is the bottom-centre edition line '2024-25', recorded as running_header for want of a footer-text role; the decorative_image is the diagonal 'NCERT / not to be republished' watermark, whose bbox encloses a rotated object. All twenty-five blocks matched by position with no null